{"name":"Silverplate","hex":"#c2c0ba","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[],"entries":[{"title":"Silverplate","blocks":[{"text":"Silverplate was the code reference for the United States Army Air Forces' participation in the Manhattan Project during World War II. Originally the name for the aircraft modification project which enabled a B-29 Superfortress bomber to drop an atomic weapon, \"Silverplate\" eventually came to identify the training and operational aspects of the program as well. The original directive for the project had as its subject line \"Silver Plated Project,\" but continued usage of the term shortened it to \"Silverplate\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Boeing_B-29_Superfortress_Bockscar_3_USAF.jpg/330px-Boeing_B-29_Superfortress_Bockscar_3_USAF.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Silverplate","wikidata":"Q7516763"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Thin_Man_ballistic_casings_at_Wendover_1.jpg/500px-Thin_Man_ballistic_casings_at_Wendover_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Thin_Man_ballistic_casings_at_Wendover_1.jpg/1280px-Thin_Man_ballistic_casings_at_Wendover_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Thin_Man_ballistic_casings_at_Wendover_1.jpg/500px-Thin_Man_ballistic_casings_at_Wendover_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"\"Thin Man\" plutonium gun test casings at Muroc Army Air Field. Casing designs for \"Fat Man\" bombs are seen in the background. The tow truck was used to lower bombs into a pit for loading into the aircraft.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThin_Man_ballistic_casings_at_Wendover_1.jpg"},{"srcset":"h